### Ballot Certification

2026 General Ballots
[2026 statewide and local ballot question language](https://elections.maryland.gov/elections/2026/ballot_questions.html)

The State Board of Elections [certified (PDF)](https://elections.maryland.gov/elections/2026/general_ballots/2026_General_Ballot_Certification_Memo.pdf) the content and arrangement of the general election ballots on August 31, 2026 pursuant to EL § 9-207(a)(2). The certified ballots are below.

Pursuant to the Supreme Court Order dated September 3, 2026, in Maryland State Board of Elections, et al. v. Lindsay Wheatley, et al. and Maryland State Board of Elections, et al. v. Michael L. Howell, et al., the language of Constitutional Amendment Question 3 now reads:

FOR the purpose of clarifying that certain requirements apply only to districts for the election of members of the Senate of Maryland and the House of Delegates; authorizing the General Assembly to grant original jurisdiction to the Supreme Court of Maryland to review the congressional districting plan of the State; and providing that nothing in the Maryland Constitution provides applicable criteria for the boundaries of a congressional districting plan.

Updated 09/03/2026

